WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.240
A liver cell and a kidney cell carry the same genome.

2
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:13.120
Yet each one reads a different set of genes, and its daughters keep reading the same

3
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:19.860
set. Eukaryotic DNA is packed into chromatin, and packed DNA is hard to read.

4
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:21.940
How does a cell choose?

5
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.560
Part of the answer is a stretch of DNA called an enhancer.

6
00:00:27.433 --> 00:00:34.033
An enhancer is DNA that raises transcription from a promoter, at a distance and in

7
00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.193
either orientation.

8
00:00:36.353 --> 00:00:41.133
Transcription factors bind it and recruit coactivators and the Mediator complex.

9
00:00:42.393 --> 00:00:47.893
Mediator bridges the enhancer to RNA polymerase II while the DNA between them loops

10
00:00:47.893 --> 00:00:54.433
out. To map one, scientists clone a region beside a promoter that drives luciferase,

11
00:00:54.753 --> 00:01:01.753
a reporter. This region of 600 base pairs holds three elements: A, B, and C.

12
00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:09.527
First, delete each element in turn and test liver cells, with each value a mean of

13
00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:14.247
repeats. Activity is scaled so the promoter alone scores 1.

14
00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.867
The full region scores 100.

15
00:01:17.947 --> 00:01:22.347
Delete A, and it still scores 95, so A is dispensable.

16
00:01:23.087 --> 00:01:27.747
Delete B, and it falls to 4; delete C, and it falls to 30.

17
00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:30.517
Now test the pieces alone.

18
00:01:31.577 --> 00:01:34.797
B alone scores 5, so B is not sufficient.

19
00:01:35.937 --> 00:01:40.717
C alone scores 2. B and C together score 90.

20
00:01:41.577 --> 00:01:46.917
If their effects added, you would expect about 6; if they multiplied, about 10.

21
00:01:47.957 --> 00:01:53.157
90 is about 9 times the multiplied guess, so B and C work together.

22
00:01:53.950 --> 00:02:00.670
Reverse B and C, and it still scores 88, so orientation does not matter here.

23
00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.030
Now try kidney cells, where nothing scores above 2.

24
00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:10.930
The simplest reading is that kidney cells lack a factor that B or C needs.

25
00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.590
A kidney repressor would also fit.

26
00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:21.733
So the minimal liver enhancer is B plus C. This fits factors on both pieces that

27
00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:26.093
must be present at once, like a committee that needs the right members.

28
00:02:26.773 --> 00:02:28.813
That is combinatorial control.

29
00:02:29.773 --> 00:02:31.453
But this is a reporter test.

30
00:02:32.113 --> 00:02:37.393
Its role at the native gene needs a test there, such as deleting B in the genome.
